From e771aa8866ef80d760f670568958a461f9ed938b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 07:50:36 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 235/410] DXF/DWG import: 3DSOLID, REGION and BODY entities
 (ACIS) become Part shapes

Neither DXF importer read the ACIS data of solids, so DWG 3DSOLIDs were lost.
Part's new AcisSat reads SAT text (the DXF form with its character cipher, versions
1.06 to 2xx as AutoCAD writes them and as LibreDWG converts the SAB of R2013+
DWGs): planes, cylinders and cones (also elliptic), spheres, tori, B-spline and
procedural surfaces by their stored B-spline, straight, ellipse and intcurve
edges, transforms (also the pre-7 form with numeric flags).  Faces are rebuilt
from the surface and the trimmed edge curves, sewn, and closed shells become
solids; problems are reported per body, never raised.

importDXF (both importers, so also DWG through dwg2dxf) adds the model space
entities as Part features "Solid_<handle>" on their layers (preference
dxfImportAcis, default on).  Corpus of 149 DWGs converted with the bundled
dwg2dxf: 80 of 81 3DSOLIDs valid closed solids, 20 of 20 REGIONs valid faces.
Not read: solids inside block definitions, and R2013+ DXF files that keep the
data in the ACDSDATA section instead of the entity.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
